<article class="env-corollary" id="C13B5F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/C13B5F">Corollary <span data-tag="C13B5F">6.3.6.7</span>.</a> Let $f: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a geometric morphism of $\infty $-topoi. Suppose that $f^{\ast }$ is fully faithful and essentially surjective on $1$-truncated objects, and that $\calX $ is $n$-localic (see §<a href="/tag/B199A1" data-tag="B199A1">6.4.5</a>). Then $f$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-topoi. </p>
